1
00:00:24,040 --> 00:00:27,080
Every time the rain no longer falls,

2
00:00:27,340 --> 00:00:29,317
and I see the sky,

3
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:35,020
I think back to when I was
a child Who could only cry,

4
00:00:35,180 --> 00:00:40,197
blindly chasing after
him I fell far behind

5
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:45,377
my only thought One day I will be stronger

6
00:00:45,460 --> 00:00:49,817
Bridery and gratitude fading with the

7
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:53,357
wind Am I stronger now than I was before?

8
00:00:53,440 --> 00:00:55,420
Or as weak as back then?

9
00:00:56,020 --> 00:00:58,677
I don't know for sure, but until I do.

10
00:00:58,760 --> 00:01:01,157
My voyage will not end.

11
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:03,277
No matter what's next!

12
00:01:03,360 --> 00:01:06,240
I'm walking straight ahead.

13
00:01:06,840 --> 00:01:08,877
So let's go!

14
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:12,557
There's nothing that can stop us now.

15
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:17,477
Though time's all on our side,
We'll never let it pull us down.

16
00:01:17,560 --> 00:01:22,557
And we may fall, But we'll
always keep on standing.

17
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:25,237
There's no way anything.

18
00:01:25,320 --> 00:01:28,737
We'll take what I hold dear away from me?

19
00:01:28,820 --> 00:01:31,257
The voices inside me.

20
00:01:31,340 --> 00:01:33,657
Push me to keep surviving.

21
00:01:33,740 --> 00:01:36,557
I'll go on, I'll get through.

22
00:01:36,640 --> 00:01:39,257
No matter what I gotta do!

23
00:01:39,340 --> 00:01:43,157
The fiercest of all can pour upon me.

24
00:01:43,240 --> 00:01:46,077
I don't care why in the world?

25
00:01:46,160 --> 00:01:48,760
Would I turn back?

26
00:01:51,720 --> 00:01:54,177
Oh, let's go.

27
00:01:54,260 --> 00:01:57,897
There's nothing that can stop us now!

28
00:01:57,980 --> 00:02:02,837
Though time's not on our side,
We'll never let it pull us down.

29
00:02:02,920 --> 00:02:07,877
And we may fall, But we'll
always keep on standing.

30
00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:14,097
There's no way anything Will take
what I hold dear away from me!

31
00:02:14,180 --> 00:02:17,680
I know the future's there for us to see.

32
00:02:29,160 --> 00:02:30,925
Make your way to the scaffold!

33
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:33,500
Watch your backs!

34
00:02:33,920 --> 00:02:35,920
The giant unit's moving out!

35
00:02:37,660 --> 00:02:39,860
They're trying to head off Oars Jr!

36
00:02:43,440 --> 00:02:45,560
Time to live up to our duty!

37
00:02:45,820 --> 00:02:47,260
He can't defeat us all!

38
00:02:51,560 --> 00:02:53,637
That thing is impossibly huge!

39
00:02:53,720 --> 00:02:56,460
He's at least twice as
big as a common giant!

40
00:02:56,780 --> 00:02:57,700
Keep shooting!

41
00:02:57,980 --> 00:02:59,333
He's a living creature!

42
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:01,220
Bullets should stop him!

43
00:03:13,380 --> 00:03:16,760
I can't say we were expecting
such a powerful beast.

44
00:03:19,160 --> 00:03:20,220
Shoot him!

45
00:03:20,420 --> 00:03:21,479
Fill up with land!

46
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:25,380
Ors, don't do this!

47
00:03:25,620 --> 00:03:27,217
You're an easy target for them!

48
00:03:27,300 --> 00:03:28,418
Please turn around!

49
00:03:29,180 --> 00:03:30,820
Hang on, Ace.

50
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:39,420
I'm coming for you!

51
00:03:50,660 --> 00:03:52,077
Ah, holy crap!

52
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:53,600
Kill that beast!

53
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:11,660
Boys, open up a path for
us to get into the bay!

54
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:17,260
Take the bay and then the plaza!

55
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:27,400
Damn it all! Fall back!

56
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:30,977
Tighten up the defensive line and
don't let them get to the plaza!

57
00:04:31,060 --> 00:04:32,680
Stand down or die, Navy!

58
00:04:34,920 --> 00:04:35,880
I swear.

59
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:38,007
What the hell are you doing?

60
00:04:38,400 --> 00:04:39,660
We're at war here.

61
00:04:39,880 --> 00:04:41,939
We don't have any use for the weak.

62
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:02,317
I've never had to crane my
head up to look at anyone!

63
00:05:02,400 --> 00:05:03,240
Me neither.

64
00:05:34,760 --> 00:05:37,797
That oars is just as
stubborn as he ever was.

65
00:05:37,880 --> 00:05:40,740
Getting yourself killed
does not make you brave!

66
00:05:40,960 --> 00:05:42,560
Don't stop me, Pops!

67
00:05:42,700 --> 00:05:43,800
I won't stop!

68
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:45,460
Cause I don't wanna!

69
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:47,060
Not until I'm done!

70
00:05:47,300 --> 00:05:48,400
Not until Serious!

71
00:05:48,740 --> 00:05:50,437
I wanna save my bro!

72
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:54,640
I want to do it now so
it doesn't hurt go there.

73
00:05:54,860 --> 00:05:56,340
I know the feeling.

74
00:05:57,280 --> 00:05:58,340
All right, men.

75
00:05:58,680 --> 00:06:00,380
Help out the big guy.

76
00:06:00,980 --> 00:06:03,100
Go cover oars. Yeah!

77
00:06:08,040 --> 00:06:10,117
Howie was supposed to fight that thing?

78
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:11,060
He's too big.

79
00:06:17,640 --> 00:06:19,169
Don't worry, Vice Admiral.

80
00:06:19,360 --> 00:06:20,860
I'll avenge you. Ah!

81
00:06:37,380 --> 00:06:39,439
Horse is one hell of a destruction.

82
00:06:39,720 --> 00:06:41,320
Let's make our move!

83
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:50,000
Slave Arrow!

84
00:06:59,060 --> 00:07:01,000
Oh! Wait, what?

85
00:07:01,260 --> 00:07:02,201
They're statues!

86
00:07:02,560 --> 00:07:04,820
So, you're the pirate empress, huh?

87
00:07:09,560 --> 00:07:11,260
What did you do to me?

88
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:12,600
I'm crumbling!

89
00:07:13,420 --> 00:07:15,260
Curfew! Deer!

90
00:07:29,700 --> 00:07:30,820
You psycho!

91
00:07:31,300 --> 00:07:33,300
Why are you attacking the Marines?

92
00:07:33,480 --> 00:07:36,617
I may have agreed to aid you in your
fight against Whitebeard's crew,

93
00:07:36,700 --> 00:07:40,760
but I don't recall making any
promises about collateral damage.

94
00:07:41,520 --> 00:07:44,560
Allies or foes, all men
are equally worthless.

95
00:07:45,340 --> 00:07:46,860
Well, except for one.

96
00:07:48,640 --> 00:07:52,537
You can hate me if you want, but you
can't say that I didn't keep my word.

97
00:07:52,620 --> 00:07:53,460
You're nuts!

98
00:07:57,400 --> 00:07:59,929
Won't you at least take
mercy on my beauty?

99
00:08:02,260 --> 00:08:03,090
Why not?

100
00:08:17,860 --> 00:08:18,740
Ah, damn it!

101
00:08:34,140 --> 00:08:37,040
I'm gonna save you now, Ace!

102
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:38,430
Stop!

103
00:08:46,860 --> 00:08:50,260
One, one, one, one, one.

104
00:09:13,020 --> 00:09:15,400
Prepare yourself for the Ursa Shock.

105
00:09:33,040 --> 00:09:34,440
Stop!

106
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:48,600
Oars, that's enough!

107
00:09:51,980 --> 00:09:53,760
You made this.

108
00:09:57,060 --> 00:10:00,413
Yeah, some folks I met in the
Wano Kingdom taught me how.

109
00:10:01,080 --> 00:10:01,940
Try it on.

110
00:10:04,500 --> 00:10:07,037
Ace ruined two others before
he got that one right.

111
00:10:07,120 --> 00:10:08,577
They burned to a crisp.

112
00:10:08,660 --> 00:10:12,425
That's what happens when someone
who's made a fire weaves straw.

113
00:10:15,980 --> 00:10:18,520
Oh, a slice of coal under here.

114
00:10:19,260 --> 00:10:20,257
Then it works.

115
00:10:20,340 --> 00:10:21,560
I like the look.

116
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:32,980
AIM AND FIRE!

117
00:10:44,120 --> 00:10:44,950
OARS!

118
00:10:45,380 --> 00:10:46,920
Run away, man!

119
00:10:47,320 --> 00:10:48,940
You're an easy target now!

120
00:10:56,140 --> 00:11:00,220
Hey, Captain Oars, what are
you doing outside in the rain?

121
00:11:03,440 --> 00:11:06,280
Rain or shine, I'm doing fine.

122
00:11:06,720 --> 00:11:08,337
I don't get wet anymore.

123
00:11:08,420 --> 00:11:10,140
Wow, I love this hat.

124
00:11:14,720 --> 00:11:16,860
If I can't save you,

125
00:11:17,120 --> 00:11:22,480
at least I can take out
one of the warlords!

126
00:11:40,420 --> 00:11:41,720
Why'd you stop?

127
00:11:42,040 --> 00:11:43,480
Ace is right there.

128
00:11:43,940 --> 00:11:45,360
Ow, my foot.

129
00:11:46,580 --> 00:11:47,410
Captain!

130
00:11:48,820 --> 00:11:50,140
Captain! Hey, Captain!

131
00:11:50,800 --> 00:11:52,859
You're going to stay outside again?

132
00:11:53,020 --> 00:11:54,360
Why should I care?

133
00:11:54,600 --> 00:11:56,760
The snow's not getting on my head.

134
00:11:57,460 --> 00:11:59,240
In the heat or the cold.

135
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:02,340
This head never gets old.

136
00:12:05,300 --> 00:12:07,300
You're the best, eh?

137
00:12:16,720 --> 00:12:18,600
Now that was fun.

138
00:12:23,740 --> 00:12:24,570
Horse!

139
00:12:44,040 --> 00:12:46,320
Wait, he's still moving?

140
00:12:46,740 --> 00:12:48,400
I thought he was...

141
00:12:49,400 --> 00:12:51,360
He's infiltrated the plaza!

142
00:12:59,960 --> 00:13:02,880
Gotta go a little bit more!

143
00:13:07,880 --> 00:13:09,297
Don't worry, Ace!

144
00:13:09,380 --> 00:13:11,340
I can make it for sure!

145
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:19,800
That damn Doe Flamingo!

146
00:13:19,980 --> 00:13:21,840
He knew I wanted ores intact!

147
00:13:22,220 --> 00:13:25,396
You don't cut the foot off
a corpse that once claimed!

148
00:13:25,620 --> 00:13:26,450
Doppelman!

149
00:13:28,260 --> 00:13:29,440
Finish him!

150
00:13:30,580 --> 00:13:32,240
Spocky Shadow Lizard!

151
00:13:34,340 --> 00:13:35,170
No!

152
00:13:51,060 --> 00:13:53,220
See, now that's how you do it.

153
00:13:53,340 --> 00:13:54,797
That is some good murder.

154
00:13:54,880 --> 00:13:56,520
No, Captain Ors!

155
00:13:56,640 --> 00:14:00,400
Damn you, you warlord scumbag! Captain!

156
00:14:01,160 --> 00:14:02,100
Ors, no!

157
00:14:30,120 --> 00:14:31,520
Arse!

158
00:14:49,740 --> 00:14:51,737
I'll have to fix up that foot of his,

159
00:14:51,820 --> 00:14:55,173
but that's a small price to
pay for another giant zombie.

160
00:14:55,460 --> 00:14:57,300
This is the foot.

161
00:15:05,520 --> 00:15:06,680
Oh, oars.

162
00:15:08,640 --> 00:15:10,960
Shouldn't drop your guard, Whitebeard!

163
00:15:25,680 --> 00:15:27,180
Bicep Hulans!

164
00:15:34,580 --> 00:15:36,100
Help me...

165
00:15:40,420 --> 00:15:41,250
Okay...

166
00:15:42,160 --> 00:15:44,925
Everybody just leave
Whitebeard alone, I guess.

167
00:15:54,960 --> 00:15:58,580
Now climb up war's body and charge!

168
00:16:28,560 --> 00:16:29,800
This is beautiful.

169
00:16:30,240 --> 00:16:31,420
To Flamingo,

170
00:16:31,680 --> 00:16:36,445
you're going to pay for what you did to
Boris, and I'm going to collect the debt.

171
00:16:36,720 --> 00:16:38,337
What the hell are you laughing at?

172
00:16:38,420 --> 00:16:39,891
How are you not laughing?

173
00:16:40,120 --> 00:16:42,944
We're standing on the
fulcrum of history itself.

174
00:16:45,420 --> 00:16:47,797
The future and past will be written here.

175
00:16:47,880 --> 00:16:49,860
Put your hammer in the dark!

176
00:16:51,400 --> 00:16:53,080
Take him down, boss!

177
00:16:53,240 --> 00:16:55,640
Stop dancing around and fight for real!

178
00:17:27,900 --> 00:17:29,540
I can't do this.

179
00:17:29,720 --> 00:17:32,073
I'm scared and I'm weak and I'm useless.

180
00:17:33,180 --> 00:17:35,945
Even our leaders are
falling one after another.

181
00:17:36,700 --> 00:17:40,288
There's no way a loser like me
is going to survive out there.

182
00:17:40,900 --> 00:17:41,730
Wait, Kuma.

183
00:17:41,860 --> 00:17:43,095
I'm running away too.

184
00:17:43,380 --> 00:17:45,027
Get back to the battlefield.

185
00:17:47,880 --> 00:17:48,762
Just let me go!

186
00:17:48,880 --> 00:17:49,740
Please, sir!

187
00:17:53,040 --> 00:17:55,020
What's Admiral Akainu doing here?

188
00:17:55,340 --> 00:17:56,760
I can't die like this!

189
00:17:56,900 --> 00:17:59,606
I'm terrified to leave
my family on their own!

190
00:17:59,780 --> 00:18:00,610
Please!

191
00:18:00,693 --> 00:18:01,557
I'm begging you, Admiral!

192
00:18:01,640 --> 00:18:02,470
Please!

193
00:18:04,720 --> 00:18:06,700
As soldiers of the Navy,

194
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:10,840
we carry the weight of the
justice of the world on our backs,

195
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:13,277
and will gladly die to defend it.

196
00:18:13,360 --> 00:18:18,300
Any man who turns tail and runs doesn't
deserve to call himself a marine,

197
00:18:18,780 --> 00:18:20,662
let alone a man for that matter.

198
00:18:20,880 --> 00:18:24,780
The most he could be
called is a waste of life.

199
00:18:28,300 --> 00:18:33,360
If you truly care about your family as
you say, you'll only shame them by living.

200
00:18:39,100 --> 00:18:39,930
No!

201
00:18:40,140 --> 00:18:42,140
He killed one of his own soldiers?

202
00:18:43,620 --> 00:18:47,160
Admiral Sakazuki, we're ready
to proceed with the operation.

203
00:18:47,880 --> 00:18:48,840
Excellent.

204
00:18:49,260 --> 00:18:50,440
It's finally time.

205
00:18:56,940 --> 00:18:58,540
The operation?

206
00:18:59,840 --> 00:19:00,800
Haze!

207
00:19:02,880 --> 00:19:05,920
I don't understand, Commander. Why?

208
00:19:06,760 --> 00:19:09,140
He's got control of my body!

209
00:19:09,560 --> 00:19:11,200
Delphamiga, you bastard!

210
00:19:13,360 --> 00:19:14,740
Stop it! Please, no!

211
00:19:20,020 --> 00:19:21,140
Pirates are evil.

212
00:19:21,400 --> 00:19:22,560
The Navy is just.

213
00:19:22,800 --> 00:19:25,682
But that's only true
because history tells us so.

214
00:19:26,180 --> 00:19:28,297
Children who've never
known peace have different

215
00:19:28,380 --> 00:19:30,968
values than children
who've never known war.

216
00:19:32,180 --> 00:19:36,340
The one who wins will rewrite the
definition of right and wrong.

217
00:19:37,060 --> 00:19:40,236
They'll decide the future
and how the past is written.

218
00:19:43,360 --> 00:19:44,940
Will justice prevail?

219
00:19:45,460 --> 00:19:47,340
Why, there's no other way!

220
00:19:50,900 --> 00:19:54,220
The winner will define
the meaning of justice.

221
00:19:55,500 --> 00:19:56,330
Go!

222
00:19:56,413 --> 00:19:58,219
Everyone get to the space oars bay!

223
00:19:59,360 --> 00:20:00,600
The bay is out!

224
00:20:02,960 --> 00:20:04,280
A knife cutter?

225
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:07,320
It's the ice witch, Wado Bay!

226
00:20:07,760 --> 00:20:10,466
I've cut plenty of
glaciers tougher than that.

227
00:20:10,700 --> 00:20:11,994
All right, let's move!

228
00:20:12,100 --> 00:20:15,640
The path is open! Right
behind you! All clear!

229
00:20:15,860 --> 00:20:17,684
It's time to move into the bay!

230
00:20:22,480 --> 00:20:25,377
They've broken through the bay
head at two different points, sir!

231
00:20:25,460 --> 00:20:29,517
There's nothing left to prevent Whitebeard's
allies from entirely flooding the area!

232
00:20:29,600 --> 00:20:32,600
I'm afraid we've got no
way to hold them back, sir!

233
00:20:32,820 --> 00:20:34,114
What should we do now?

234
00:20:35,080 --> 00:20:36,315
Don't worry about it.

235
00:20:39,040 --> 00:20:39,870
We're ready.

236
00:20:40,120 --> 00:20:41,591
Put the plan into action.

237
00:20:41,740 --> 00:20:43,080
It's about time.

238
00:20:43,320 --> 00:20:44,520
Out of the way!

239
00:20:44,800 --> 00:20:46,340
Either stand down or die!

240
00:20:46,820 --> 00:20:48,055
Move it, you old bag!

241
00:20:49,740 --> 00:20:51,060
I can't wash!

242
00:20:51,420 --> 00:20:52,637
I can't put out the dry!

243
00:20:52,720 --> 00:20:54,640
I feel so fresh and clean!

244
00:20:54,740 --> 00:20:57,975
Sorry, boys, maybe try again
in a couple hundred years.

245
00:20:58,420 --> 00:21:00,832
Put a call out to all ships and soldiers.

246
00:21:15,160 --> 00:21:17,860
Of course, he's got a plan up his sleeve.

247
00:21:18,860 --> 00:21:21,880
You've always been
resourceful, Buddha Sengoku.

248
00:21:26,700 --> 00:21:27,600
Old man!

249
00:21:28,780 --> 00:21:30,368
What are you doing up here?

250
00:21:30,640 --> 00:21:32,757
Not having second thoughts, are you?

251
00:21:32,840 --> 00:21:34,660
No, they chose to be pirates.

252
00:21:34,960 --> 00:21:36,960
They brought this upon themselves.

253
00:21:37,580 --> 00:21:39,140
In that case... Shut up!

254
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:43,560
I don't want to talk.

255
00:21:44,060 --> 00:21:45,620
I just want to sit here.

256
00:21:54,580 --> 00:21:55,500
Little idiot!

257
00:21:57,160 --> 00:21:57,990
Morons!

258
00:21:58,073 --> 00:22:00,297
I don't want either of
you becoming pirates!

259
00:22:00,380 --> 00:22:01,615
Hey, don't hit Luffy!

260
00:22:01,900 --> 00:22:04,020
Mean old fart! Oh, what?

261
00:22:04,460 --> 00:22:05,920
Ace, you come here!

262
00:22:08,020 --> 00:22:10,540
I have no sympathy in me for criminals.

263
00:22:14,960 --> 00:22:17,300
But family is a different story.

264
00:22:18,620 --> 00:22:19,640
Now what?

265
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:21,700
What am I supposed to do?

266
00:22:26,100 --> 00:22:31,420
Ace, you fool Why couldn't you have just
listened to me and done what I asked?

267
00:22:46,200 --> 00:22:48,300
Ace, trust me on this.

268
00:22:48,640 --> 00:22:50,780
You two really should join the Navy.

269
00:22:52,380 --> 00:22:53,210
Okay?

270
00:22:55,460 --> 00:22:58,080
I know you'll make a strong Navy soldier.

271
00:23:15,360 --> 00:23:18,337
If you're feeling any doubt
over what must be done,

272
00:23:18,420 --> 00:23:21,185
I'm afraid I just can't
take pity on you, Garp.

273
00:23:22,160 --> 00:23:25,460
If I had doubts, I would
have done something already.

274
00:23:25,940 --> 00:23:28,017
Did you hear what I just heard, Helmepo?

275
00:23:28,100 --> 00:23:29,460
What their strategy is?

276
00:23:30,100 --> 00:23:30,930
Yeah.

277
00:23:31,013 --> 00:23:34,697
They're going to bypass the schedule
and immediately execute Firefist Ace.

278
00:23:34,780 --> 00:23:36,220
But if they do that...

279
00:23:36,780 --> 00:23:37,610
Huh?

280
00:23:37,693 --> 00:23:39,100
What the...

281
00:23:43,780 --> 00:23:44,610
Hm?

282
00:23:44,693 --> 00:23:45,523
What is that?

283
00:23:45,606 --> 00:23:47,261
Something's falling from the sky!

284
00:23:47,620 --> 00:23:50,796
It's gotta be another surprise
ambush from Whitebeard!

285
00:24:12,380 --> 00:24:15,260
You just have to overdo it every time!

286
00:24:15,700 --> 00:24:17,577
This is because of his death wing!

287
00:24:17,660 --> 00:24:19,240
Oh, so it's all my fault?

288
00:24:19,420 --> 00:24:20,597
Who cares whose fault it is?

289
00:24:20,680 --> 00:24:21,597
We're gonna die!

290
00:24:21,680 --> 00:24:23,320
It's all frozen down there!

291
00:24:33,500 --> 00:24:35,860
Oh, yeah, I'm rubber. I'll be fine.

292
00:24:36,100 --> 00:24:38,580
Hey, what about us, you selfish jerk?

293
00:24:38,760 --> 00:24:39,897
Do something already.

294
00:24:39,980 --> 00:24:42,237
This is not how I picture myself dying.

295
00:24:42,320 --> 00:24:43,900
Somebody help me, please.

296
00:24:44,260 --> 00:24:48,197
I still care about whose fault this
is, and it's all yours, Straw Hat.

297
00:24:48,280 --> 00:24:49,280
Damn you, though.

298
00:24:51,000 --> 00:24:52,080
I'm hearing.

299
00:24:53,820 --> 00:24:55,220
Please!
